findings.fix:
Remove the manual replace and let JSON.stringify handle escaping:
```tsx
// Replace this line
const baseUrl = (process.env.OMNIBRIDGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL ?? "https://omnibridge-dev.vercel.app/api/v1").replace(/"/g, "\\\"");
// With this
const baseUrl = process.env.OMNIBRIDGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL ?? "https://omnibridge-dev.vercel.app/api/v1";
```
The dangerouslySetInnerHTML block can stay the same, as JSON.stringify will correctly produce a quoted string.
